\par\par \b \uc2 Argentine stocks down on banks, bonds flat   \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 23:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, June 11 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks fell on Monday as investors shed bank issues due to strong yields on U.S. Treasuries, and some benchmark bonds also took a hit from the Treasury yield.   \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of 16 leading stocks gave up 0.33 percent to close at 2,162.1 points. Volume on the broad market was moderate at $32.9 million with 37 gainers, 37 losers and 15 issues unchanged.   \par \par \uc2 Banco Hipotecario fell 2.54 percent to 3.07 pesos while BBVA Banco Frances lost 1.3 percent to 11.4 pesos per share.   \par \par \uc2 "It's evident that our market continues highly sensitive to the ups and downs on Wall Street. The strong rate (for U.S. Treasuries) plays against us and means a lack of institutional investors," said Marcelo Paccione, analyst with ConsulCapital business consulting company in Buenos Aires.   \par \par \uc2 Yields on the benchmark 10-year U.S. Treasury notes <US10YT=RR> were at 5.15 percent on Monday, at levels not seen since July last year. Higher yields in developed markets historically lead to investors shifting cash away from riskier emerging markets.   \par \par \uc2 On the local bond market the dollar-denominated Discount bond's price edged down 0.2 percent <ARDISCD=RASL> in over-the-counter trade, while the Par bond lost as much as 2.2 percent percent <ARPARA3=BA>. But on average, bond prices were flat.   \par \par \uc2 "If the rate on the 10-year (Treasury) returns to 5 percent (Argentine) bonds could recover," said Florencia Pique, analyst with Compania Inversora Bursatil investment firm.   \par \par \uc2 The peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed unchanged at 3.0950/3.0975 per U.S. dollar in trade between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses <ARSB=>, while it rose 0.08 percent to 3.0725/3.0750 per dollar in formal interbank trade <ARS=RASL>, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily to prevent appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070611e36b0021s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
