\par\par \b \uc2 Argentine stocks near record high; peso gains   \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2007\par 23:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES, May 21 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks rose for a fifth straight session on Monday, nearing a record close on rising banking shares and regional markets.   \par \par \uc2  The MerVal index <.MERV> of 16 leading stocks gained 1.03 percent to 2,209.08 points, accumulating a 3.83 percent gain since Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  "While regional markets remain firm, the MerVal is recovering its liquidity and inching closer to its highest values of the year," said Dionisio Corneille, director of the brokerage of the same name.   \par \par \uc2  "The market's climb is being supported by banking shares, particularly Banco Macro and Banco Hipotecario," he added.   \par \par \uc2  The MerVal closed at an all-time high on April 16 at 2,224.83 points.   \par \par \uc2  On Monday, broad market volume was moderate at 91.6 million pesos ($29.4 million). Of active issues, 46 rose, 21 fell and 18 were unchanged.   \par \par \uc2  Banco Macro  shares rose 4.07 percent to 11.5 pesos while Banco Hipotecario  climbed 4.35 percent to 3.12 pesos.   \par \par \uc2  Macro shares have risen since the company announced on Thursday that it was issuing up to $100 million in peso-denominated bonds.   \par \par \uc2  The peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened in trade between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses, at 3.1125/3.115 per dollar <ARSB=> and rose 0.08 percent to 3.0725/3.0750 per dollar in formal trade between banks <ARS=RASL>, which is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .       \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA000002