\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks follow regional markets lower  \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2007\par 22:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Jan 26 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks dipped for a second straight day on Friday, falling in tandem with regional markets hit by a slump in U.S. equities.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal <.MERV> index of 15 leading stocks shed 0.22 percent to close at 2,039.46 points, accumulating a 1.5 percent loss over the past two sessions. The index has lost 2.44 percent since Jan 1.  \par \par \uc2 "There was little volume, which indicates investors stayed away given the volatility in other markets," one trader said.  \par \par \uc2 In Chile, the all-market IGPA <.IGPA> slipped 0.30 percent while Sao Paulo's Bovespa index <.BVSP> fell 0.61 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Steelmaker Siderar led losers on the MerVal, dropping 2.7 percent to 21.6 pesos, followed by Banco Macro which fell 1.52 percent to 10.05 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume remained thin at 42.1 million pesos ($13.5 million), up slightly from 40.3 million pesos on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 In local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in trading between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses, the Argentine peso weakened 0.16 percent to 3.122/3.12515 per U.S. dollar <ARSB=>.  \par \par \uc2 In formal trade between banks, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  competitive for exports, the peso fell 0.24 percent to 3.105/3.108 per dollar <ARS=RASL>.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said heavy dollar demand from importers helped drive the peso lower despite heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-