\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks post second straight record close  \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2006\par 22:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES, Dec 27 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks climbed to a record close for the second straight day on Wednesday as investors snapped up shares that had lagged amid recent gains, traders said.  \par \par \uc2  The MerVal index <.MERV> of the 13 leading stocks rose 1.4 percent to 2,089.32 points and posted a new intraday trading high of 2,091.71 points.  \par \par \uc2  Trade volume was moderate at 68.9 million pesos ($22.3 million).  \par \par \uc2  "The market is being helped by the optimistic outlook in external markets," said Claudio Szlaien, an analyst at Marlon Financial Resources.  \par \par \uc2  Ruben Pascuali, a trader at Mayoral Bursatil, said investor interest was directed at shares in foodmaker Molinos , oil company Petrobras Participaciones  and steel maker Acindar .  \par \par \uc2  Molinos rose 5.75 percent to 3.86 pesos, Petrobras Participaciones gained 1.79 percent to 3.42 pesos and Acindar rose 1.67 percent to 4.85 pesos.  \par \par \uc2  On \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso weakened amid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and as private investors bought greenbacks, traders said.  \par \par \uc2  In trade between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses, the peso <ARSB=> fell 0.16 percent to close at 3.09/3.0925 per U.S. dollar. In interbank trade, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso weakened by the same amount to close at 3.0725/3.075<ARS=RASL>.       \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ARGENTINA|LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061227e2cr00195\par 