\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weaker On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Mixed  \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2006\par 21:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso weakened Monday for a second straight session as heavier \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent the market a signal that the government plans to maintain a weak peso.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, bonds were mixed amid steady trading.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended the day at ARS3.0775 against the U.S. dollar, weakening from Friday's close at ARS3.0725. The peso's slide "was a consequence of anticipation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and not permit the dollar to further weaken," said Carlos Lizer, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at local brokerage Puente Hermanos. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local market, buying dollars to build reserves while maintaining a weaker peso that favors Argentine exports.  \par \par \uc2 But stronger demand for pesos from overseas investors seeking locally traded bonds this month gave the peso a sharp boost against the dollar. From October's close at ARS3.09 against the dollar, the peso had strengthened to ARS3.0675 last Thursday, Nov. 9.  \par \par \uc2 Lizer said he expects that the peso reached a ceiling, and will remain weaker than ARS3.07 to the dollar for the remainder of the year.  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, the price of the benchmark Discount bond in pesos continued to gain ground, recently reaching ARS134.60, up from Friday's close at ARS134.40, while the Par in pesos was down slightly to ARS50.70 from ARS50.80.  \par \par \uc2 So-called GDP warrants, which were stripped out of restructured debt late last year, were also mixed, with the peso warrant at ARS11.05, down from ARS11.20, and the dollar coupon under New York legislation at ARS38.40, up from ARS38.15.  \par \par \uc2 Argentina's Economy Ministry announced Friday that the peso-denominated gross domestic product-linked securities will pay ARS0.65 per ARS100 of notional, while dollar-warrants will pay ARS0.62.  \par \par \uc2 The December payment uses 2005 as a reference year.  \par \par \uc2 The peso coupon "is paying less than expected," said Alejandro Barros, an analyst with local Banco Piano. Barros had expected an ARS0.67 payment for the peso warrants.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 13-11-06 2028GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061113e2bd001a8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
