\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Hits ARS3.105/Dlr On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ;Bonds Dn  \b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2006\par 17:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2006, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Sep 06, 2006 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso continued to lose ground on the dollar Wednesday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought more dollars to edge the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deeper into a three-year weak spot.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS3.1050 against the dollar, after hitting the ARS3.1000 point on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue," said Carlos Lizer, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local brokerage Puente Hermanos. "This is basically in line with our estimate that by the end of the year we'll see a dollar between ARS3.10 and ARS3.13."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  habitually buys dollars to build reserves and maintain a weak peso that favors Argentine exports.  \par \par \uc2 The end of the annual soy harvest, which brings heavy dollar inflows from exporters, has made it easier for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday's close marks the peso's weakest point since mid-March 2003, when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid as far as ARS3.1250 against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, prices were "mostly down, possibly on some profit taking after yesterday," said Diego Zavaleta, an analyst with local Besfamille Sociedad de Bolsa. Volume was weak for a second day, he added.  \par \par \uc2 Among sliders, the benchmark Discount in pesos was down to ARS126.50 from ARS126.90, while the Par in pesos was down to ARS49.30 from ARS49.80.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier Wednesday, the Economy Ministry called an auction for $500 million in new seven-year, dollar-denominated BONAR VII bonds.  \par \par \uc2 Bids for the new 2013 BONAR VII bonds will be accepted until 2 p.m. (1700 GMT) Thursday, with an issue on Sept. 12. The sale will include competitive and noncompetitive bids. The BONAR VIIs come due in 2013 and carry a 7% coupon. The auction follows a this year's BONAR V series of five-year 2011 bonds. The BONAR V program authorizes $1.5 billion in issuance, with two separate tranches of $500 million each coming to market so far.  \par \par \uc2 "There is room for shorter-term dollar bonds," Zavaleta said. "There is the Boden 2012 and beyond that the long-term Pars and Discounts in dollars." Argentina initially issued $15.5 billion in Boden 2012s during the nation's 2001-02 financial crisis.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 09-06-06 1534ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020060906e2960023q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
