\par\par \b \uc2 DJ REPEAT&CORRECT: Argentina Peso Hits ARS3.10/Dlr; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2006\par 18:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2006, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Sep 05, 2006 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 (The item "\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  Peso Hits ARS3.10 On \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Up -2-" published at 3:47 p.m. EDT, omitted paragraphs 1-5.)  \par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso hit the ARS3.10 mark against the dollar Tuesday, its weakest point in three years, on heavy last-minute dollar buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, locally traded bond prices were higher across the curve, albeit amid mild volumes.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS3.10, weakening from ARS3.0950 on Monday, amid normal volumes. Tuesday's close marks the peso's weakest point since mid-March 2003, when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid as far as ARS3.1250 against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  habitually buys dollars to build reserves and maintain a weak peso that favors Argentine exports. Officials, including Economy Minister Felisa Miceli, have recently reiterated their defense of this plan.  \par \par \uc2 Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped reporting its daily dollar buying in July, local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Hector Blanco of local brokerage ABC Mercado de Cambio estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought roughly $80 million during the last 15 minutes of the session to push the peso into weaker territory.  \par \par \uc2 Miceli said Monday that regular dollar buying will continue, estimating that without steady \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the peso would strengthen to ARS2.30 against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 In addition to recovering the $9.5 billion that the government tapped in January to entirely pay down its debt with the International Monetary Fund, daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely increase total reserves on the year as President Nestor Kirchner heads toward his 2007 re-election bid, Blanco said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's late dollar buying Tuesday came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars earlier in the day.  \par \par \uc2 "It sold cash dollars at ARS3.0950, ARS3.0960 this morning and then at the last minute paid cash at ARS3.0990," Blanco said. "There must have been some financial transaction that isn't clear at the moment."  \par \par \uc2 Total volume in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market reached $237 million.  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, "prices are generally all up," said Paulino Seoane, an analyst in Buenos Aires with Lopez Leon Brokers.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark Discount in pesos was up to ARS126.85 from ARS126.60, while the Par in pesos was up to ARS49.75 from ARS49.60. At the shorter end of the curve, the Bocon Pre 12, another peso note, was also higher at ARS176.20 from ARS175.50.  \par \par \uc2 Peso notes are linked to inflation. The government announced late in the session Tuesday that the consumer price index rose 0.6% in August, higher than a 0.5% increase predicted last week by economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \uc2 Among dollar notes, the Boden 2012 was up to ARS287.80 from ARS287.40.  \par \par \uc2 "There's not much volume, as usual," Seoane added.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 09-05-06 1620ET  \par \par \uc2 Dok