\par\par \b \uc2 Argentine stocks steady with volume at 3-year low  \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2006\par 23:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina (Reuters) - Argentine stocks ended steady Monday and trade volume dwindled to a three-year low in the absence of guidance from U.S. markets, closed for the country's Labor Day holiday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark MerValindex of 12 leading shares closed just 0.02 percent lower at 1,677.49 points. MerVal shares are up 8.7 percent since the start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was meager at 8.5 million pesos ($2.7 million), its lowest level since September 2003 when a U.S. holiday sent trade tumbling to 4.4 million pesos.  \par \par \uc2 "Today's session does not lend itself to much analysis, since trading continues to be limited and this was exacerbated by the lack of deals on Wall Street," said Jorge Alberti, a trader at online brokerage ElAccionista.com.  \par \par \uc2 The session's losses were led by energy transmission company Transener, the shares of which fell 1.4 percent to 1.44 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso ended unchanged at 3.095/3.0975 per dollar in a quiet session. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which buys dollars almost daily to keep the peso weak, did not appear to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|FUN  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060904e294001dx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
