\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weakens On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Rebound  \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2006\par 17:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2006, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Aug 30, 2006 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso weakened slightly as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed dollar buying Wednesday, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to its weakest point against the dollar since March 2003.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, bond prices rose and volume nearly doubled as investors took positions after a recent slide.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS3.0975 against the dollar, weakening from Tuesday's close at ARS3.0950. Total volume was also higher in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, reaching $319 million. The peso hit ARS3.0975 on Monday, leading the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to abstain from its habitual dollar buying on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's return to the market Wednesday demonstrated "that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't worried about the peso's current price," said Gustavo Quintana, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local Lopez Leon Brokers. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars to build reserves and maintain a weak peso that favors Argentine exports.  \par \par \uc2 The peso was further weakened as banks sought dollars to close positions at the month's end, Quintana said.  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, volumes were on track to nearly double from rock-bottom levels seen Tuesday, said Javier Salvucci, an analyst with Silver Cloud Advisors.  \par \par \uc2 "Longer-term dollar bonds are doing especially well," he added. Among these, the Par bond under U.S. jurisdiction was recently quoted at ARS135, up from ARS132.00 at Tuesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 Among peso notes, the Bocon Pro 12 was at ARS175.75, up from from ARS175. "The Pro 12 is seeing the day's biggest volume after being punished in recent sessions," Salvucci said.  \par \par \uc2 The local bond market took its lead from U.S. government securities, which saw prices rally after the successful auction of $14 billion in five-year Treasury notes.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 08-30-06 1553ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020060830e28u001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
