\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Bonds Mixed; Peso Weaker On More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2006\par 21:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentine bond prices were mixed Wednesday amid mild volumes, while the peso continued to slide against the U.S. dollar on steady \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The peso slid to ARS3.0875 against the dollar, weakening from ARS3.0850 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The local bond market early last week saw stronger prices and a return of foreign investors on better-than-expected U.S. economic data and a growing belief among investors that the Fed's two-year tightening cycle was over.  \par \par \uc2 After light profit-taking during the past few sessions, the local market lacked a clear tendency, said Sebastian Di Nucci, a portfolio manager with local FDI Consultants.  \par \par \uc2 The restructured par in pesos stood out as the day's best performer, albeit amid thin trading. The par in pesos was recently quoted at ARS49.20, up from ARS48.70.  \par \par \uc2 Di Nucci said the local market will remain in a lull until it becomes clear where the U.S. economy is going. "Although the Fed stopped raising interest rates this month, I think they could continue to raise them again next month," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Among local sliders, the discount in pesos was at ARS126.45, down from ARS127.10, while the dollar-denominated Boden 2012 was at ARS285.50, from ARS285.66. The Bogar 2018, a peso note, was up slightly to ARS147.20 from ARS147.10. These three note typically account for about half of the local market volume.  \par \par \uc2 In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, "it was similar to yesterday, with total volume reaching about $256 million," said Gustavo Quintana, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local Lopez Leon Brokers.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars in the final half hour of the session Wednesday, pushing the peso into slightly weaker territory against the dollar, he added. Quintana sees \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushing the peso to the ARS3.1000 against the dollar, with the exchange rate possibly hitting ARS3.0900 by week's end.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 23-08-06 1919GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060823e28n000zy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
