\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks climb as U.S. data boost markets  \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2006\par 23:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Aug 16 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks climbed higher on Wednesday, boosted by investor optimism that U.S. interest rates will remain unchanged in the short term, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of 12 leading shares rose 0.63 percent to 1,634.10, pushed up by gains in steel sector stocks.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was a moderate 48 million pesos ($15.5 million).  \par \par \uc2 "The MerVal was helped by gains in external markets, with most buys focusing on steel stocks," said Juan Diedrich, an analysts at Capital Markets Argentina.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. consumer prices, excluding food and energy, rose less than expected in July, the U.S. Labor Department said on Wednesday, a day after producer prices were reported to have risen only slightly.  \par \par \uc2 Investors worry higher U.S. rates could draw investment away from emerging markets like Argentina.  \par \par \uc2 On the MerVal, steel tube maker and index heavyweight Tenaris climbed 3.33 percent to 56.85 pesos while steelmaker Siderar rose 2.07 percent to 21.70 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> closed steady at 3.095/3.0975 to the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept up its steady \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060816e28g001p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
