\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks dip in thin trade, peso steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 226 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2006\par 23:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Aug 11 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks slid on Friday, tracking U.S. markets in a session marked by investor caution and thin trade, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of 12 leading shares lost 0.85 percent to close at 1,618.88 points, racking up a 5.66 percent loss over the last six sessions.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume fell to one of its lowest levels in a year at 24.2 million pesos ($7.8 million).  \par \par \uc2 "The market is reaccommodating and sagging due to external markets," said Guido Macchi, a trader at the Macchi, Julio brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 On Wall Street, the Dow Jones industrial average <.DJI> shed 0.33 percent over investor worries about slower U.S. economic growth and disappointing news from chip makers dragged tech stocks lower.  \par \par \uc2 Leading Argentine banking conglomerate Grupo Financiera Galacia led losers on the MerVal, falling 1.69 percent to 1.75 pesos, followed by power transmission company Transener , which was off 1.41 percent to close at 1.40 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> held steady at 3.09/3.0925 to the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept up its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060811e28b0029z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
