\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Bonds Mixed; Peso Weaker On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2006\par 18:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2006, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Aug 07, 2006 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 Argentine bonds remained mixed Monday, as longer-duration bonds continued to see higher prices, while investors moved away from shorter notes linked to inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the peso closed at ARS3.0725 against the dollar, slightly weaker than Friday's close at ARS3.0700.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar instruments continued to do well in the local bond market, with the Boden 2012 bond recently quoted at ARS286.75, up from ARS286 Friday. So-called GDP warrants in dollars under U.S. jurisdiction were at ARS29.00 from ARS28.60, while dollar warrants under Argentine law were at ARS25.89 from ARS25.60.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark Discount bond in pesos was also higher, reaching ARS124.30 from ARS124. At the shorter end of the curve, however, peso notes linked to the consumer price index continued to fade after the government reported last week that the CPI rose by 0.6% in July on the month. "With inflation waning, people are losing interest in (inflation indexed) bonds," said Alejandro Barros, an analyst with local Banco Piano.  \par \par \uc2 In part, investors are moving from shorter-term bonds to floating-rate Nobac notes that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions on a weekly basis. Meanwhile, a recent change in reserves requirements has led banks to offer more attractive interest rates on longer-term accounts to draw depositors from checking and other current accounts, Barros said. As of Aug. 1, banks are required to hold 19% of depositors' checking and savings account funds in reserve at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , up from 17% for these "sight," or current, accounts.  \par \par \uc2 In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso weakened on late \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Overall volume was around $250 million, said Carlos Lizer, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local brokerage Puente Hermanos.  \par \par \uc2 Demand for pesos from cereal exporters repatriating overseas dollar earnings has begun to wane now that the annual soy harvest has wrapped up, Lizer said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 08-07-06 1600ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020060807e28700263\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
