\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks slide on Tenaris profit-taking  \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2006\par 23:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Aug 4 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks closed lower on Friday as investors pocketed profits in heavyweight Tenaris a day after the company reported better-than-expected second-quarter earnings.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of 12 leading shares slid 1.86 percent to 1,683.90 points, with Tenaris falling 3.88 percent to close at 59.45 points.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was moderate at 48.6 million pesos ($15.7 million), with more than half in the steel tube maker.  \par \par \uc2 ""Profit-taking in Tenaris hit the market hard," said Claudio Szlaien, an analyst at Marlon Financial Resources.  \par \par \uc2 Tenaris , the world's largest manufacturer of seamless pipes for the oil industry, said on Thursday its second-quarter net profit rose more than 45 percent to $495.8 million.  \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> strengthened 0.08 percent to close at 3.0975/3.10 to the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept up its usual regular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060804e284002qc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
