\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks gain in thin trade, peso steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2006\par 23:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, July 31 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks edged higher on Monday as investors shuffled their portfolios in a session marked by thin trade.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of 12 leading shares rose 0.7 percent to 1,701.58 points, ending the month down 0.56 percent. Still, the index has risen 10.26 percent since Jan. 1.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was slack at 23.8 million pesos ($7.7 million).  \par \par \uc2 "There were no institutional investors and few buyers, so the market had little to move on," said Juan Diedrich, an analyst at Capital Markets Argentina. "A rebound in Tenaris helped nudge the market upward."  \par \par \uc2 Tenaris , the world's largest manufacturer of seamless pipes for the oil industry, closed 2.23 higher to 59.70 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> closed flat at 3.1025/3.105 pesos per dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars to help \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  meet upcoming debt payments.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the peso weak to stimulate exports.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ARGENTINA|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060731e27v002du\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
