\par\par \b \uc2 Argentine stocks inch up as U.S. rate worries fade  \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2006\par 23:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, July 3 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks closed higher for the fourth straight session on Monday as investor concerns over U.S. interest rate hikes appeared to dissipate, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of 12 leading shares inched up 0.85 percent to 1,725.78 points, accumulating a 7.95 percent gain since Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "It was a slow climb but reflected a slight change in investors' moods," said Diego Zavaleta, a trader at Besfamille brokerage, referring to recent investor worries over U.S. Federal Reserve rate increases.  \par \par \uc2 Franciso Marra, a trader at Bull Market Brokers, added: "It's premature to say that confidence has been completely restored, but there's been an important change."  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was slack at 34.7 million pesos ($11.2 million), in large part because of the upcoming Fourth of July holiday in the United States.  \par \par \uc2 Tenaris shares rose 1.29 percent to end at 62.80 pesos while steelmaker Acindar advanced 0.65 percent to 4.64 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> gained 0.32 percent to close at 3.0875/3.09 to the dollar in light trading marked by heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|U|RBN|M|D|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060703e273001w3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
