\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Argentina stocks end at record high on Tenaris gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2006\par 22:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with trader quote, details)  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, April 24 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks closed at a new high for the fourth time this month on Monday, led by steel tube maker Tenaris, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark MerVal <.MERV> index of 11 leading shares rose 1.26 percent to close at 1,943.07 points, breaking the last high of 1,924.80 reached on April 18.  \par \par \uc2 Shares of Tenaris , the world's biggest producer of tubes for the energy industry and an index heavyweight, climbed 4.18 percent to 72.3 pesos amid investor enthusiasm over the company's medium-term outlook, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "Everything is being pushed by Tenaris, which appears to be in a sort of bubble and unaffected by a correction in international oil prices," said Francisco Marra, a trader at Bull Market brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. crude futures ended almost $2 lower on Monday on profit-taking after prices hit a record above $75 on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Also among winners was steelmaker Acindar , which rose 1.38 percent to 5.14 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal has notched a 7.9 percent gain this month and is up 25.9 percent since Jan. 1.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume in Buenos Aires was moderate at 65.8 million pesos ($21.4 million), down from Friday's 85.8 million pesos.  \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso <ARSB=> maintained its tendency to firm slightly against the dollar, due to the abundant supply of dollars being sold by exporters, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed up 0.33 percent from the previous close at 3.0725/3.075 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 So far this month, the peso has gained 0.57 percent against the dollar, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to keep the peso weak by buying greenbacks.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market almost daily to help keep exports competitive and traders said the peso would have risen more strongly without that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060424e24o001yc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
