\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks, peso slump on U.S. rate hikes  \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 22:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, March 21 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks slumped and the peso sank to a three-year low on Wednesday amid investor concerns about possible rises in U.S. interest rates, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of the 11 leading shares fell 0.72 percent to 1,793.09 points, accumulating a 4.61 percent gain for the month and rising 16.18 percent since January.  \par \par \uc2 Volume was light at 57.1 million pesos ($18.5 million).  \par \par \uc2 "There was some profit-taking," said Horacio Corneille, head of the brokerage firm carrying the same name.  \par \par \uc2 "But the session leaves me a bit concerned because stocks didn't react the same way as other international markets."  \par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the Bovespa <.BVSP> closed 0.68 percent higher while the Dow Jones <.DJI> ended up 0.73 percent.  \par \par \uc2 On the MerVal, steelmaker Siderar led losers, falling 1.52 percent to 26 pesos. Acindar , another steelmaker, also dropped 1.49 percent to 5.29 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 Recent comments by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke have fanned investor expectations of possible rate hikes to cool economic growth and tame inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Investors worry higher U.S. interest rates could lure cash from emerging markets.  \par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso <ARSB=> fell to a three-year low on Wednesday as local investors dumped Argentine bonds and bought dollars, attracted by higher yields in the U.S. market, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed 0.32 percent lower at 3.0925/3.095 per dollar, its lowest level since March 17, 2003, when it hit 3.11 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Private banks were selling positions in government bonds due to declines in recent days and they were the ones buying dollars," said Fernando Izzo of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  house ABC Mercado de Cambios.  \par \par \uc2 The peso has lost 1.45 percent of its value so far this year, helped by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the peso weak for exporters.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060322e23m001pt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
