\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Gains Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Lull  \b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 17:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2006, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Mar 15, 2006 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.)  \par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso edged stronger Wednesday, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as exporters and banks sought the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, bonds hit a lull as prices held flat or inched into weaker territory amid low volume, following in part rising U.S. Treasury rates.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended the day at ARS3.0725 against the dollar compared with Tuesday's close at ARS3.0775. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slowly strengthened against the dollar this week, gaining a full centavo from Friday's close at a three-year weak-point.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported later Wednesday that it bought $30 million and EUR40 million during the day's session. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held off on its habitual dollar buying on Monday and Tuesday, but surprised the market Tuesday by purchasing EUR50.5 million. "It's a sly strategy because the market watches dollars," said trader Fernando Izzo of local ABC Mercado de Cambio.  \par \par \uc2 Buyers were mainly investors, exporters repatriating overseas dollar earnings and private banks, he added.  \par \par \uc2 Liquidity has tightened this week, with the overnight call money rate reaching 10.5% Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Analyst Javier Salvucci of local Silver Cloud Advisors attributed the call money rate rise to an announcement from the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday night. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked minimum reserve requirements for bank's savings and checking deposits and ended the practice of paying interest on those funds.  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, volume was thin, with notes at the shorter end of the curve losing some ground. Among sliders, the Bocon Pre 12, a pre debt-swap peso note, was down to ARS179.75. Restructured longer term notes in pesos were unchanged, with the discount steady at ARS52 and the par at ARS127.  \par \par \uc2 Salvucci said shorter-term bonds could be losing on some arbitrage to long-term Nobac certificates auctioned weekly by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The long-dated Nobac notes have rates tied to the "Badlar" average of 30-day certificate of deposit rates and are expected to benefit from Monday's reserves requirement change.  \par \par \uc2 In Tuesday's certificates auction, the 728-day Nobac paid 5.0206% over Badlar, or 12.9581% in absolute terms, compared with 12.6773% last week.  \par \par \uc2 The rising Badlar reflects a move by banks to attract more savers to its longer-term fixed deposits. That rate is expected to rise further once the new reserve requirement rules come into effect April 1.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson and Kim-Mai Cutler, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 03-15-06 1634ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020060315e23f008lh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
