\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Flat On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Resume Upswing  \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 15:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2006, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Mar 10, 2006 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso held at a three-year low for a second-straight session Friday, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engaging in last-minute dollar-buying to offset a mild uptick in demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as foreign investors returned to the local bond market.  \par \par \uc2 Locally traded bonds gained ground as U.S. Treasurys began to recover from an early session slide on strong U.S. jobs data for the month of February.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended at ARS3.0825 against the dollar, after reaching ARS3.0800 just 10 minutes before market close.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in at the last minute to hold the peso," said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Gustavo Quintana of local Lopez Leon Brokers. Although official data wouldn't be available later, Quintana estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought on a par with Thursday's $41 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Quintana attributed renewed demand for the peso to returning investors. "The stronger (Brazilian) real also helped," he said.  \par \par \uc2 In the local debt market, bonds went on the upswing after a week of profit-taking. Among rebounders, the restructured par bond in pesos was recently quoted at ARS52.40, up from Thursday's close at ARS52.00. Also, the discount in pesos, the heaviest traded note Friday, was up at ARS127.40 from Thursday's close at ARS126.40.  \par \par \uc2 Overall, volume was up on the day but remained moderate, according to analyst Leonardo Chialva of local Delphos Investments.  \par \par \uc2 "I believe in the next week we're going to see a bond market that is recuperating from its recent fall," Chialva said. "We'll see the market revalue these bonds."  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson and Kim-Mai Cutler, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 03-10-06 1455ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020060310e23a0081n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
