\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks gain on selective buys, peso slips  \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2006\par 22:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Feb 27 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks gained on Monday in choppy trade as investors rejigged portfolios at the end of the month, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of the leading 11 shares climbed 0.55 percent to 1,736.22 points for a cumulative gain so far this year of 12.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Investors were cautious, trader said, and steelmaker Tenaris continued to dominate in otherwise slim trade.  \par \par \uc2 Volume was 61.6 million pesos ($20 million) and Tenaris accounted for about a quarter of that total.  \par \par \uc2 "It's worrisome to not see more volume. It could be due to lack of interest by foreign investors but the dependence on Tenaris is especially bothersome," said Horacio Coneille, head of the Horacio Coneille brokerage firm.  \par \par \uc2 Tenaris , which makes seamless steel tubes for the oil industry and reports earnings on Wednesday, slipped 0.10 percent to 49.20 pesos but was still up nearly 30 percent since the start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> fell 0.16 percent against the dollar in quiet trade as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying stopped the peso from firming, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 3.0775/3.08 per dollar, accumulating a depreciation of 0.97 percent so far this year.  \par \par \uc2 "We foresee an exchange rate limited to its current value under strong \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a report by Argentine Research, a consulting firm.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars to rebuild its reserves after Argentina paid off its entire debt to the IMF. It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the peso weak for export purposes.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060227e22r001xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
