\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks rebound in heavy trade, peso flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2006\par 22:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Feb 16 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks rebounded on Thursday as investors picked up lower priced blue-chip shares after a recent slump, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of the leading 11 shares climbed 1.58 percent to close at 1,695.64 points after sliding 2.82 percent since Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was a robust 203 million pesos ($66 million), one of the highest levels in peso terms in nearly a decade.  \par \par \uc2 "We've had a lot of days in negative territory and the market reacted. This is more of a rebound than a general tendency," said Mariano Tavelli, a trader at Tavelli y Compania brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 Heavyweight Tenaris , which makes steel tubes for the petroleum industry, paced winners, gaining 3.6 percent to 46.1 pesos. Steel maker Acinder also rose 1.53 percent to 5.32 pesos after announcing earlier in the day that its net profit in 2005 inched up less than 1 percent because of labor and iron ore costs.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> closed flat at 3.0825/3.0850 to the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060216e22g002bq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
