\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks fall on options expiration  \b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2006\par 22:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Feb 14 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks retreated on Tuesday as investors speculated in blue chips ahead of the expiration of futures options, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of the leading 11 shares fell 0.19 percent to close at 1,669.7 points, for a cumulative loss of 6.93 percent in February.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was a moderate 78.7 million pesos ($25.5 million).  \par \par \uc2 "The options expiry on shares in Acindar and Petrobras pushed the Merval lower," said Francisco Marra, a trader at Bull Market Brokers.  \par \par \uc2 Investors face a Thursday deadline for exercising stock options.  \par \par \uc2 Oil firm Petrobras Participaciones was among the losers, falling 1.63 percent to 3.62 pesos. Steelmaker Acindar also fell 0.57 percent to 5.2 pesos, along with Telecom , which lost 2.9 percent to 7.38 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> closed virtually flat at 3.0825/3.0850, steadied by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060214e22e0034l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
