\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Bonds Fall, Peso Down On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2006\par 22:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Updates in ninth paragraph with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data from the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .)  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Locally traded Argentine bonds dropped slightly Monday as market participants took profits from the strong rallies they posted last week.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the peso weakened slightly to close at ARS3.07 to the dollar, down from ARS3.0675 on Friday, after last-minute \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "There was a bit of profit-taking but volumes were pretty good," said Noelia Lucini, an analyst at Capital Markets Argentina. She said last week's rallies in Argentine sovereign debt, when bonds were helped by a strong auction of 30-year U.S. Treasurys and later by a rally in Brazilian bonds on the back of a buy-back announcement, gave way to "corrections" Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Moreover, she said, expectations for a moderation in consumer prices following last week's confirmation of an outbreak of foot-and-mouth disease in Argentina, which is expected to drive down beef prices, have softened peso-denominated inflation-indexed bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The discount bond in pesos was last quoted at ARS130.85, down 0.34% on the day. The par in pesos had fallen even further, sliding 1.12% to ARS53.15. Both bonds are indexed to an inflation indicator known as CER.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar bonds, which were especially helped by the Brazil-led narrowing in Argentina's yield spread to Treasurys last week, were more stable. The Boden 2012 was down just 0.04% at a dollar equivalent ARS285.00.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, trading was confined for most of the day to a very narrow range in thin volumes, holding tightly to the ARS3.0675-to-the-dollar level it had closed at Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Then, in the last few minutes, traders said, the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market with bid for dollars whose size exceeded the market's total offering. This pushed the peso to a weaker close of ARS3.07.  \par \par \uc2 After the close, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it bought $54.5 million in the open market Monday and EUR1 million.  \par \par \uc2 Ever since Argentina tapped $9.5 billion in reserves to pay down its debt to the International Monetary Fund in early January, the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has vowed to use \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to recuperate reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Still, traders were surprised to see it enter the market at such late notice Monday. The peso remains close to three-year lows, which means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is paying a high price for its dollars. Moreover, the weak valuations mean the basic objective of the federal government - for a competitive exchange rate - has already been met, they say.  \par \par \uc2 Hector Blanco, a trader at ABC Mercado, said \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as Monday's added to the unpredictability of policy. And that, he said, has driven participants out of the market, pushing down volumes.  \par \par \uc2 "No one wants to take positions in this market," Blanco said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Michael Casey, Dow Jones Newswires; michael.j.casey@dowjones.com; 54-11-4313 1918 [ 13-02-06 2145GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060213e22d0011w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\pi