\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Ctrl Bk Head Defends Policy,Lauds Credit Growth  \b0\par\par\uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2006\par 17:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Martin Redrado used an op-ed article heralding the long-awaited recovery of bank lending in the country to defend his institution's policies Monday.  \par \par \uc2 In an article published by business daily El Cronista, Redrado said bank credit, which was severely depressed after the financial crisis of 2001 and 2002, had marked its "definitive" recovery in recent months.  \par \par \uc2 He attributed this to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of providing incentives for lending while at the same time maintaining a "firm control of risks in the financial system."  \par \par \uc2 These policies, he said, had been accompanied by the necessary precondition of a "prudent monetary policy" marked by a rapid accumulation of international reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Redrado's defense of his institution's policies comes as criticism of it rises among private economists.  \par \par \uc2 Critics argue that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserve accumulation policy is the flip-side of a federal government-backed policy of keeping the peso weak through foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 This, they say, has helped fuel rising prices in \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it has promoted imported inflation and has resulted in mass issuance of domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has expanded the money supply in an inflationary way.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's failure to achieve its inflation target for 2005 - consumer prices rose 12.3% last year, more than four percentage points above the ceiling rate for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target band - reflects a loss of independence in policy-making, these critics say.  \par \par \uc2 Redrado did not directly address these criticisms in his article but he nonetheless made a strident defense of his policies.  \par \par \uc2 He argued that policy positions at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have encouraged a reduction in banks' exposure to government debt have reduced the "crowding out" factor from government borrowing, promoted private sector lending and at the same time inherently bolstered the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence.  \par \par \uc2 "The financing of government constitutes one of the criticisms that has always been leveled when the independence of central banks in emerging countries is evaluated," Redrado said. "In such countries, excessive holdings of public debt on the part of banks implies an assumption of risks that can result in perverse behavior once the moment to reduce position arises."  \par \par \uc2 Rerado said banks' exposure to public sector debt has fallen from 40% to 31% of the total sector's assets over the past 12 months, which he said was accompanied by a sharp increase in lending to the private sector.  \par \par \uc2 While he welcomed this development, Redrado said more work was needed to get lending rates above the low 10% of gross domestic product currently seen in Argentina.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced new measures on Sunday aimed at boosting housing loans. The measures would expand the collateral banks can use as guarantees against lending for home construction.  \par \par \uc2 Banks can now accept rights to structured trust fund vehicles that invest in construction projects in lieu of direct mortgages over a piece of property.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Michael Casey, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4313 1918; michael.j.casey@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 06-02-06 1619GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060206e226000sk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
