\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Argentine stocks close slightly higher,peso off  \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2006\par 22:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Repeating to make clear in headline that stocks closed higher)  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Jan 25 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks inched higher on Wednesday amid selective trading and profit-taking by institutional investors, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of the 11 leading stocks climbed 0.61 percent to 1,708.41, accumulating a gain of 10.7 percent since the beginning of the year. Volume was 82.1 million pesos (26.7 million).  \par \par \uc2 "There was a bit more open play in the market with less business concentrated in Tenaris and more money in other stocks," said Jorge Alberti, an analyst with online brokerage ElAccionista.com. "That's why we saw the climb."  \par \par \uc2 Tenaris, the MerVal's standout stock recently, has climbed steadily with rising world oil prices. Shares in the company -- which makes steel tubes for the petroleum industry -- fell 3.14 percent on Wednesday to 46.20 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 "It was mostly profit-taking," said Sergio Del Guidice, a trader at the Del Guidice brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> weakened 0.08 percent to close at 3.0725/3.075 to the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2  (REPEAT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|U|RBN|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060125e21p0023b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
