\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Bonds Rally;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Holds Peso Flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2006\par 21:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2006, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Jan 24, 2006 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 Locally traded Argentine bonds rallied Tuesday, with prices for restructured pesos notes wading into record territory.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the peso ended flat for a second straight day at ARS3.0375 against the dollar amid steady \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The bond market picked up today," said Noelia Lucini, a fixed income analyst with Capital Markets Argentina. With about an hour left in trading "it has slowed some, but is still doing well," she said. Among gainers, the restructured discount bond in pesos was up to a high ARS123.10 from ARS122.30 on Monday, while the par in pesos was up to ARS51.05 from ARS50.50.  \par \par \uc2 Among the day's few lackluster performers was the dollar-denominated Boden 2012, last quoted at ARS282.75 from Monday's close at ARS283.00. The Argentine government announced in the Official Bulletin on Tuesday that it will sell Venezuela an additional $312.4 million in Boden 2012s. The sale will be carried out by way of a direct placement "at market price" through Venezuela's choice of financial agents, the government said. Economy Ministry officials have said they plan to issue between $2 billion and $3 billion in new debt this year, adding that they will tap Venezuela as a buyer if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 Argentina turned to Venezuela last year after the market largely rejected a low-ball nominal interest rate the government offered for a dollar-denominated Boden 2015 fixed-price auction. Venezuela bought more than $1 billion in Argentine bonds last year.  \par \par \uc2 In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, "it was a repeat of yesterday," according to Gustavo Quintana, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local Lopez Leon Brokers. Volumes were similar to Monday and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy on par with the previous day's purchase of $64 million. Official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data will be available later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 01-24-06 1433ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020060124e21o00a6z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
