\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks, peso close steady in light trade  \b0\par\par\uc2 221 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2006\par 22:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Jan 24 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks closed virtually unchanged on Tuesday in a choppy and lightly traded session.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of the 11 leading stocks declined 0.06 percent to 1,697.92 points, slipping after opening the session higher. Since Jan. 1, the MerVal is up 10.02 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Volume was a moderate 89.6 million pesos ($29.1 million).  \par \par \uc2 Traders said selective buying was helping some stocks rise but it wasn't carrying over to the market as a whole.  \par \par \uc2 "We're seeing a weak market without much air to inch above 1,700 points," said Francisco Prack, the chief economist at SBS brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 Tenaris , the world's leading maker of steel tubes for the oil industry, continued to gain, rising 0.85 percent to 47.7 pesos. The company has a 24 percent weighting in the MerVal.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say high world oil prices and the prospect of a South American natural gas pipeline have sparked interest in Tenaris in recent months.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> closed steady at 3.07/3.0725 to the dollar amid \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060124e21o001wf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
