\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Stronger As  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Lulls; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2006\par 22:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso gained ground on the dollar for a second-straight day as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently continued to abstain from its almost daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the open market.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a handful of inflation-linked peso bonds were gaining in an otherwise quiet market.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended the day at ARS3.0525, stronger than Tuesday's close at ARS3.0600. "Demand for pesos hasn't changed," said Carlos Lizer, the head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local brokerage Puente Hermanos. Instead, "yesterday and today the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and (state-run) Banco de la Nation have not been present," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Overall, trading remained thin in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. "January, especially during the first two weeks, has lower-than-normal volume," Lizer added. Despite its temporary absence, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to return to regular dollar buying to rebuild reserves the government tapped to pay down its $9.5 billion debt with the International Monetary Fund last week, and to maintain a weak peso that favors Argentine exports.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's steady \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which pumps new pesos into the market, comes as \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  struggles with rising inflation that increased by just over 12% for the full year in 2005. Part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strategy to pull pesos out of the system is its weekly auction of short-term Lebac and Nobac certificates. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported late Tuesday that this week's 1.2-billion-peso ($392.15 million) Lebac auction was oversubscribed, although there was again a heavy concentration of bids in the shortest end of the rate curve.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the total ARS1.333 billion amount accepted was insufficient to roll over all the ARS1.527 billion in Lebacs expiring this week. Based on the discounted value of bids accepted, some ARS205 million in excess liquidity was not absorbed. Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to roll over ARS324 million in expiring Lebacs, after a ARS1.35 billion auction drew bids worth just ARS1.174 billion. Yet again this week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again seemed reluctant to let interest rates rise in order to draw in more buyers in all but the longest-dated instrument.  \par \par \uc2 Rising consumer prices, in turn, have continued to fuel demand for locally traded bonds linked to inflation. During Wednesday's session, investors focused on a handful of inflation-linked peso bonds, said Adolfo Zuberbuhler, an analyst with local Banco Finansur. Among gainers, the restructured discount in pesos was last quoted at ARS120.90, up slightly from 120.00, while the pre-debt swap Bogar 2018 was up to ARS141.60 from ARS141.40, and the Bocon Pro 12, another pre-restructuring peso note, was at ARS181.00 from ARS180.50.  \par \par \uc2 Beyond these three bonds, "the rest of the market is calm," Zuberbuhler said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 11-01-06 2119GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060111e21b000v4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\