\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weaker On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2006\par 22:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $70 million)  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso ended slightly weaker against the dollar Wednesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to buy dollars to offset demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from investors seeking locally traded bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended the day at ARS3.0400 against the dollar, off slightly from Tuesday's close at ARS3.0375.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Fernando Izzo of local brokerage ABC Mercado de Cambio said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars throughout the day's session. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported later that it bought $70 million during the day's session, bringing total reserves to $18.673 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which pumped some ARS213 million pesos into the system on Wednesday alone, came a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weekly auction of short-term Lebac and Nobac certificates was undersubscribed due to high year-end liquidity needs and low interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has struggled with its weekly auctions, raising worries about its ability to control inflation. The government's statistics agency reported after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market close that the consumer price index rose by 1.1% month-on-month in December, bringing full-year inflation to a whopping 12.3%.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts see monetary policy becoming more difficult to manage since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to use steady daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to recover the $9.5 billion in foreign reserves it tapped on Tuesday to entirely repay Argentina's debt with the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, bonds "have begun the new year very well," said Noelia Lucini, an analyst with Capital Markets Argentina. "This has more to do with better Treasury rates, which have helped emerging markets in general," she said. The inflation data, which were leaked at midday to a local television news channel, also helped boost demand for peso-denominated bonds linked to inflation, Lucini added.  \par \par \uc2 Among gainers, the restructured discount bond in pesos was last quoted at ARS120.30, up from ARS119.30 on Tuesday, while the par in pesos was at ARS50.50, up from ARS50.20. Dollar bonds also did well, with the pre-debt swap Boden 2013 up at ARS250.90 from ARS249.65, and the Boden 2012 at ARS276.50, up from ARS275.00.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 04-01-06 2157GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060104e214000ro\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
