\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Gains On Dlr Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ;Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2005\par 21:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Dec 22, 2005 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso gained on the dollar Thursday, boosted in part by investors seeking the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy locally traded bonds, which also saw gains.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended the day at ARS3.0225 against the dollar, a full centavo stronger than Wednesday's close at ARS3.0325. Hector Blanco, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local brokerage ABC Mercado de Cambio, said that the market has recovered from last week's announcement that the government plans to entirely pay down its $9.8 billion debt with the International Monetary Fund. With business returned to normal, "traders are struggling to determine where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set its target to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trigger will likely remain weaker than ARS3.00, based on what President Nestor Kirchner told a group of industrial business leaders Wednesday. Kirchner said the peso would trade between ARS3.00 and ARS3.05 to the dollar in 2006, weaker than the ARS2.95-2.98 rate pegged in the government's budget proposal for next year.  \par \par \uc2 The Kirchner administration has actively maintained a weaker peso in a bid to boost exports, which sparked Argentina's economic recovery in 2003 and remain strong. Many analysts believe the peso is undervalued and would strengthen significantly without almost daily \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Blanco estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought between $15 million and $30 million Thursday, up from $12 million on Wednesday. Official data would be available later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 During Kirchner's Wednesday meeting, he also asked the industry leaders to keep prices steady and to continue increasing investment. Inflation, projected to hit 12% by year-end, has become the administration's top macroeconomic concern.  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, "just about everything was up, although volumes were thinner," said Alejandro Barros, a financial analyst at local Banco Piano. Investors are coming back to the local bond market after initial concerns about the IMF debt paydown announcement because "the economy is doing well and next year looks to be another good year, although inflation remains a concern."  \par \par \uc2 Among gainers, the restructured discount bond in pesos was last quoted at ARS117.80, up from ARS116.00 on Wednesday, while the par in pesos was at ARS48.80, up from ARS48.00. Moving to the middle of the curve, the peso-denominated Bogar 2018 was up at ARS145.85 from ARS145.60, while shorter-term bonds were largely unchanged, Barros said.  \par \par \uc2 Markets will be open Friday, although it is a holiday for government employees. Traders expect very thin volumes.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 12-22-05 1505ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020051222e1cm00b41\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
