\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks fall on cenbanker talk, peso dips  \b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2005\par 22:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Dec 6 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks slid over 2 percent on Wednesday ahead of a national holiday amid lingering talk that the country's central banker might resign, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of 12 leading stocks retreated 2.12 percent to close at 1,525.53 points, falling after opening the session in positive territory.  \par \par \uc2 Volume was a slack 61.7 million pesos ($20.7 million).  \par \par \uc2 "The market heated up with the Redrado rumor. We're in a nervous market and any rumor leads to sell-offs," said Oscar Campos, a trader at InterValores brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 Local markets will be closed on Thursday in observance of the Immaculate Conception holiday.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation that Martin Redrado, the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , might quit first circulated last week after President Nestor Kirchner named Felisa Miceli as economy minister to replace Roberto Lavagna in a Cabinet reshuffle.  \par \par \uc2 Redrado's office has dismissed the rumors.  \par \par \uc2 Steel tube maker Tenaris was among the stocks that lost ground, falling 3.34 percent to 36.20 pesos while Siderar dipped 2.96 percent to 24.60 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso <ARSB=> closed steady at 2.9825/2.9875 per dollar, down 0.08 percent as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to offset dollar inflows from exporters, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051207e1c7001tb\par }\page