\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Bond Rally Steams Along; Peso Steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2005\par 23:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Updates with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raising repo rate) \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Locally traded Argentine bonds continued to rally Friday, with investors snapping up GDP warrants, the special coupons tied to economic growth that stripped out restructured bonds this week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The peso closed the trading day virtually unchanged at ARS2.9825 against the dollar, little changed from ARS2.9800 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "Bonds are trying to reach levels seen before (former Economy Minister Roberto) Lavagna's exit" was announced on Monday, said Hernan Korin, a local portfolio manager with Supervielle Asset Management. "I think there was an overreaction to his departure and now bonds are recovering. Investors are especially interested in the GDP coupons today."  \par \par \uc2 Before trading separately on Wednesday, the peso-denominated coupons had traded in the gray market around ARS4.60. But they slid to ARS4.20 on the news that Lavagna would be replaced by former Banco de la Nacion President Felisa Miceli. The market perceived Miceli, whose credentials and experience aren't as strong as Lavagna's, as being easily manipulated by Argentina's populist President Nestor Kirchner.  \par \par \uc2 Among gainers Friday, the restructured discount bond in pesos was last quoted at ARS118.00, up from ARS116.60, while the par in pesos was at ARS47.80 from ARS47.60. The GDP coupons, meanwhile, were higher at ARS5.00.  \par \par \uc2 Korin warned that market volatility will remain a concern in the near term. "The market is very sensitive to rumors right now," he said. Chief among them has been swirling talk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Martin Redrado plans to step down after being passed over for the economy minister job.  \par \par \uc2 In the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, it was a slower day as cereal exporters didn't repatriate much of their overseas dollar earnings, said Claudio Arar, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with Banco Itau in Buenos Aires. "Some days are just busier than others," Arar said. He said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently stepped in to buy some dollars. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported later that it bought $50.5 million in the open market, up from $44 million Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's varied activity this week - from selling dollar futures to stop a run on the peso in the wake of Lavagna's exit announcement to buying dollars to check the peso's recovery - which shows that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  between ARS2.97 and ARS3.00 against the dollar, Arar said. "That's the range that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems pleased with," he said.  \par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market close, the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its reference rate for transactions in the securities repurchase, or repo, market at the same time that it took the somewhat contradictory action of easing liquidity conditions for banks by lowering minimum cash ratios.  \par \par \uc2 Although the news emerged about 15 minutes before the local bond market closed, Supervielle's Korin said the reaction was negligible. He speculated that the move could free up more money to buy bonds - especially inflation-linked shorter-term notes that are expected to draw investors. Argentina's statistics agency Indec is slated to release November consumer price index data on Monday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most recent consensus forecast predicts a 0.8% month-on-month rise from October, although Korin said some are expecting a figure closer to 1.0%.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 02-12-05 2211GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051202e1c2000wp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
