\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks fall in slow trade, peso firms  \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2005\par 21:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Nov 15 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks dropped on Tuesday in a slow session characterized by the absence of institutional investors, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal <.MERV> index of the 12 leading stocks fell 1.38 percent to 1,572.84 points after two days of small gains. The index is up 14.4 percent so far this year.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was similar to Monday's at 46.6 million pesos ($15.6 million).  \par \par \uc2 One of the biggest losers was Banco Frances , which dropped 2.1 percent to 7.57 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 "With no relevant news, the market has nothing to take it higher, especially after company results were generally not as good as expected," said Francisco Marra, trader at Bull Markets Brokers.  \par \par \uc2 The Argentine market is looking at events abroad this week, such as the U.S. consumer price index on Wednesday and developments in Brazil amid speculation that the finance minister will resign.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso <ARSB=> gained 0.17 percent against the dollar to close at 2.9775/2.98 despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the peso weak for export purposes.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051115e1bf0028b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
