\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Redrado:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Driving Inflation  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Michael S. Derby  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2005\par 20:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president defended his bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies and said they are not creating inflation pressures in his country.  \par \par \uc2 Martin Redrado, at a conference held by the Bank of Mexico in Mexico City Tuesday, said, "I don't see there is a conflict there as long as we sterilize" the bank's moves to buy dollars to build up his nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Redrado was addressing a question from the audience that sought to understand whether these \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are fueling price pressures in his nation. Economists expect inflation to come in a 11.2% gain for the year in Argentina, well over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ceiling of 8%.  \par \par \uc2 The central banker hung some of the blame for current levels of inflation on the past policies of his bank, and noted that there's a lag before the bank's currently restrictive policies will impact the price pressure environment. He added, "we are exactly on track" in terms of the bank's monetary policy goals.  \par \par \uc2 -By Michael S. Derby, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4192; michael.derby@dowjones.com [ 11-15-05 1444ET ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020051115e1bf0003s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
