\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Stronger Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2005\par 20:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso continued to rebound Tuesday, gaining nearly a centavo on the dollar despite the return of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, locally traded bonds followed U.S. Treasurys higher on solid volume.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended the day at ARS2.9650 against the dollar, stronger than Monday's close at ARS2.97625.  \par \par \uc2 Volumes were up significantly from Monday as cereal exporters exchanged overseas dollar earnings and investors sought pesos to buy bonds, said Hector Blanco, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local ABC Mercado de Cambio.  \par \par \uc2 To slow the peso's appreciation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in as the main dollar buyer. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased between $50 million and $80 million, Blanco estimated. That would be a notable increase from the $18.5 million the bank bought on Monday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  habitually buys dollars in a bid to maintain a weaker peso that favors Argentine exports, but has only bought a total $43 million since Oct. 19. The peso weakened late last month on emerging market pessimism that has since cleared. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to report its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data later Tuesday. [ 08-11-05 1944GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, notes "continued to rise. More than anything, this was a result of what's happening with yields on U.S. Treasurys," said Sebastian Di Nucci, an analyst with local InvertirOnline. In mid-afternoon trading, the yield on the benchmark 10-year U.S. Treasury was around an intraday low of 4.56%, compared with 4.57% earlier Tuesday and 4.64% late Monday in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The restructured Argentine discount bond in pesos was seeing the heaviest volume, Di Nucci said, and it was last quoted at ARS129.25, up from ARS127.70 on Monday. The par in pesos was also was also rising, up to ARS50.30 from ARS49.90.  \par \par \uc2 Investors were also interested in dollar notes, with the Boden 2013 rising to ARS242.35 from ARS241.59.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson and Clarisse Douaud, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 08-11-05 2002GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051108e1b80015b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
