\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks slip on earnings, peso steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2005\par 22:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Nov 8 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks fell for a second straight day on Tuesday amid investor disappointment over third-quarter earnings reports from some blue-chip companies, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal <.MERV> index of the leading 12 stocks slid 1.9 percent to close at 1,615.59 points. On Monday, the index slumped 1.9 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Volume was a moderate 69.5 7 million pesos ($23.3 million).  \par \par \uc2 "The MerVal keeps responding to earnings reports that have been seen as mostly regular," said Dionisio Corneille, a trader at the firm of the same name. The index "is continuing with its correction and respecting the 1,570 to 1,580 point range."  \par \par \uc2 Banco Frances sank 3.39 percent to 7.40 pesos a day after reporting net earnings of 86.2 million pesos ($29.1 million), which was below investor expectations, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso <ARSB=> closed steady at 2.9825/2.985 to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051108e1b80028h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
