\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks fall, peso at 14-month low  \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2005\par 23:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Oct 27 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks lost ground on Thursday in heavy trade on investor jitters about possible U.S. interest rate hikes, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal <.MERV> index of the leading 12 stocks slid 1.99 percent to 1,577.67 points, accumulating a loss of 6.9 percent in October but still up 14.7 percent so far in 2005.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was strong at $129.3 million pesos ($42.8 million).  \par \par \uc2 "The Merval's trend was set by foreign markets. Money is leaving emerging markets and that is leaving its mark," said Ricardo Maied, analyst with Federal Bursatil brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve holds its next policy meeting on Tuesday and is widely expected to raise official interest rates for the 12th straight time.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's benchmark stock index Bovespa <.BVSP> fell 2.01 percent and Mexico's bourse <.MXX> was off 1.46 percent.  \par \par \uc2 In Buenos Aires, steelmaker Siderar plunged 4.55 percent to 25.15 pesos on downbeat forecasts for its third-quarter earnings due to an upturn in costs.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso fell 0.58 percent to a 14-month low as foreign banks heavily bought dollars, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <ARSB=> closed at 3.015/3.0175 per dollar, after breaking the 3-per-dollar mark on Wednesday for the first time in weeks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months to prevent the peso from strengthening, did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday or Thursday.  \par \par \uc