\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks slide 1.46 pct on U.S. rate fears  \b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2005\par 23:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Oct 18 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks fell on Tuesday, in step with leading regional market losses amid concerns about further interest rake hikes in the United States, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of 12 leading stocks slid 1.46 percent to 1,589.97 points, adding to its loss of 6.2 percent so far this month.  \par \par \uc2 Volume was a moderate 65.7 million pesos ($22.1 million).  \par \par \uc2 "Inflation concerns in the United States have again cast uncertainty over emerging markets," said Hernan Labrone, analyst at Fenix Compania Financiera.  \par \par \uc2 Higher U.S. interest rates means less foreign capital enters high-yielding but riskier emerging markets.  \par \par \uc2 In Mexico City, the IPC index <.MXX> shed 1.29 percent and Brazil's Bovespa <.BVSP> fell nearly 4 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Among the losers in local trading, steel tubemaker Tenaris fell 4.5 percent to close at 32.90 pesos. The company's shares are off 17.75 percent this month after chalking up gains most of the year.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso <ARSB=> closed 0.25 percent weaker at 2.9675/2.97 pesos per dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with purchases of $105.3 million, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051018e1ai0024s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
