\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Bonds Continue Rebound, Peso Flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2005\par 22:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $105.3 million)  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Locally traded Argentine bonds saw more gains Tuesday as investors continued to flow back into the market after moving away from emerging market debt earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the peso ended flat on the day at ARS2.9700 against the dollar, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cranked up its regular dollar buying to dampen a similar rebound seen by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Bonds were "all going up," said fixed income analyst Noelia Lucini of Capital Markets Argentina. "They aren't going up as much as yesterday, but the tendency remains positive."  \par \par \uc2 Among gainers, the restructured discount in pesos was last quoted at ARS123.75, up from ARS123.00 on Monday, while the par in pesos was at ARS49.40 from ARS49.00. The Boden 2014, a peso note predating this year's debt restructuring, was also up, to ARS99.30 from ARS97.80.  \par \par \uc2 "If there is no adverse international news, the recovery will likely continue," Lucini predicted. Investors will also be watching out for any changes in public spending or economic plans following midterm congressional elections this Sunday, she said.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported later that it bought $105.3 million during the day's session.  \par \par \uc2 Operating volume was also high, at more than $300 million during the day's session, said Hector Blanco of local ABC Mercado de Cambio. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood out for a second straight day as the lone dollar buyer in the market, he added.  \par \par \uc2 "With the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  determined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the only thing that's left for the market to do is to decide at what price to step in," Blanco said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson and Clarisse Douaud, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 18-10-05 2040GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051018e1ai000zh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
