\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks inch higher, boosted by Brazil  \b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2005\par 23:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Sept 23 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks closed slightly higher on Friday, moving in line with Brazilian shares and falling just short of another historic high, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of 11 leading stocks rose 0.39 percent to close at 1,658.84. The index has accumulated a gain of 1.9 percent this week and 20.6 percent so far this year.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was a brisk 87.5 million pesos ($30 million).  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's Bovespa index <.BVSP> gained 2.01 percent on Friday, boosting stocks in neighboring Argentina, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal has notched new record highs five times in September, thanks to robust economic growth and stability in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate.  \par \par \uc2 "You can see that the MerVal will meet resistance in the short term and we could see a small correction towards 1,610 points," said Sebastian Di Nuchi, an analyst with Invertir Online.  \par \par \uc2 "Today's gains were attributable largely to a rise in Tenaris shares on speculation about what could happen with Hurricane Rita," Di Nuchi added.  \par \par \uc2 Tenaris gained 1.7 percent to a record 36.60 pesos. The company, which is controlled by Argentina's Techint, benefits from surging oil prices as the world's largest producer of seamless steel tubes for the oil industry.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso <ARSB=> closed unchanged at 2.91/2.9125 per dollar thanks to ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the peso weak for exports.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E